        <body>
            <div xml:id="d309">

                <pb facs="0613" n="517" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg517"/>

                <head>No. 307.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">General Schenck to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-06-11"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 11, 1874</date>.
                        (Received June 22.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 577.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to Mr. Moran’s No. 473 and to
                    Lord Derby’s note to him of the 26th of March last, relative to the existence of
                    a traffic in slaves carried on between Tripoli and Constantinople through Malta,
                    I <pb facs="0614" n="518" xml:id="pg518"/> have now to send you, inclosed
                    herewith, a further communication from his lordship, with a copy of a dispatch
                    on the subject from Her Majesty’s consul-general at Tripoli.</p>
                <p>This correspondence, while it tends to show a desire and endeavor on the part of
                    the British government in good faith to suppress or discourage this clandestine
                    traffic, discloses also the fact that practices are admitted to still prevail at
                    Tripoli which are, in effect, a continuing connivance there with the detested
                    trade, and that this connivance of the Turkish, authorities is somehow
                    successful and beyond the efforts of the officials at Malta to detect or
                    prevent.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>ROBT. C. SCHENCK.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d309-a1.xml" xpointer="d309-a1"/>
